NOTICES

The licensor cannot revoke these freedoms as long as you follow the license terms.

This dataset is derived from SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) imagery. The
underlying satellite data may be subject to the terms of the original data
provider (e.g., ESA Copernicus/Sentinel-1 open access license). Users are
responsible for verifying compliance with any upstream data source terms.

CC BY 4.0 is a data/content license, not an OSI-approved software license (no
patent grant, no explicit source-distribution mechanics). It was chosen
deliberately over a software license (e.g. MIT) to keep one single license
for the whole repository, and because attribution — central to citing this
dataset in academic work — is a hard requirement of CC BY but not of more
permissive software licenses.

For the full legal text of CC BY 4.0, see:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
